@startuml
title 4G (LTE) Architecture — E-UTRAN + EPC + IMS (Class Diagram Style)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
left to right direction

package "UE" {
  class UE {
    + USIM
    + IMSI
    + NAS Signaling
  }
}

package "E-UTRAN (RAN)" {
  class eNodeB {
    + Radio Scheduling
    + Handover
    + AS Signaling (RRC)
  }
}

package "EPC (Evolved Packet Core)" {

  class MME {
    + Control Plane
    + Mobility Mgmt
    + Auth orchestration
    + Bearer setup (signaling)
  }

  class SGW {
    + User Plane anchor
    + GTP-U forwarding
    + Mobility anchor (data)
  }

  class PGW {
    + Internet gateway
    + UE IP allocation
    + NAT/Charging hooks
  }

  class HSS {
    + Subscriber DB
    + Auth vectors
    + Subscription profile
  }

  class PCRF {
    + Policy control
    + QoS rules
    + Charging policies
  }
}

package "IMS (VoLTE Services)" {
  class "P-CSCF" as PCSCF {
    + SIP Proxy
    + First IMS hop
  }

  class "S-CSCF" as SCSCF {
    + SIP Serving node
    + Call control
  }

  class "IMS App Server" as IMSSRV {
    + TAS/AS logic
    + Supplementary services
  }
}

package "External Networks" {
  class "Internet / DN" as INET
  class "PSTN / Legacy Voice" as PSTN
}

' ---------------------------
' Interfaces / Connections
' ---------------------------

UE --> eNodeB : LTE Air\n(AS: RRC/PDCP/RLC/MAC/PHY)

' Control Plane
eNodeB --> MME : S1-MME\n(NAS signaling)
MME --> HSS : S6a\n(Authentication,\nSubscriber profile)

' User Plane
eNodeB --> SGW : S1-U\n(GTP-U user data)
SGW --> PGW : S5/S8\n(GTP-U)
PGW --> INET : SGi\n(IP traffic)

' Policy control
PGW --> PCRF : Gx\n(Policy/QoS rules)

' IMS / VoLTE
UE --> PCSCF : SIP signaling\n(VoLTE)
PCSCF --> SCSCF : SIP core
SCSCF --> IMSSRV : Service triggers
IMSSRV --> PSTN : Interconnect\n(optional)

note bottom
This is a "pure class" PlantUML diagram:
- Uses only classes/packages/associations
- Guaranteed to render without allowmixing/component keywords
end note
@enduml